      "message": "Empirically.\n\nFirst, they are components of project names where non-Apache2 code is allowed per http://go/android3p . Second, I looked at the paths to all of the NOTICE and LICENSE files on the 3 AOSP hosts, and I chose these to eliminate any partial path that could be model a number or product name.\n\nThe -a flag, the ability to customize the build, and the proposed rollout with partner outreach will give partners an opportunity to intercede before anything gets displayed in any UI.\n\nI don\u0027t see anything in your comment to suggest the approach is unsound.",
